; engines.node in package.json names one exact patch, and npm's engine-strict
; defaults to false -- so without this line a mismatched Node prints
; EBADENGINE and installs anyway. Verified: node:24-alpine warned and then
; resolved all 116 packages regardless. This turns that warning into exit 1,
; which is the difference between the pin being a note and being a rule.
;
; The cost is deliberate: `npm ci` now refuses on any Node that is not the
; pinned patch, including for a moment after a Renovate bump. A host carrying
; some other Node builds the frontend in the pinned image instead of arguing
; with this file -- the README gives the one-liner.
;
; tests/test_toolchain_versions.py asserts both that this file says so and
; that the Dockerfile copies it in before `npm ci`, since npm only reads an
; .npmrc that is actually in the directory it installs from.
engine-strict=true
